        "title": "Mississippi State&#8217;s Josh Hubbard Named Preseason All-SEC First Team",
        "content": "<p>Mississippi State linebacker Josh Hubbard was selected to the Preseason All-SEC First Team by media members, the league announced Monday. The honor comes ahead of this week&#8217;s SEC Media Days.</p>\n<p><em>Source: <a href=\"https://hailstate.com/news/2026/10/12/mens-basketball-hubbard-secures-all-sec-preseason-media-first-team\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Original Article</a></em></p>\n",
        "excerpt": "<p>Mississippi State linebacker Josh Hubbard was named to the Preseason All-SEC First Team by league media, announced Monday ahead of SEC Media Days.</p>\n"
      },
      "patch": {
        "title": "Mississippi State’s Josh Hubbard Named Preseason All-SEC First Team",
        "excerpt": "Mississippi State men’s basketball guard Josh Hubbard earned preseason first-team All-SEC honors in the league’s media voting announced Oct. 12.",
        "content": "<p>Mississippi State men’s basketball guard Josh Hubbard was named to the media’s preseason All-SEC first team Monday, Oct. 12, ahead of SEC Media Days, according to Mississippi State Athletics.</p>\n<p>Hubbard joins Quinndary Weatherspoon as the only Bulldogs with three career preseason All-SEC selections. The Madison native enters the 2026-27 season with 1,947 career points, fourth in school history, and a program-record 311 made 3-pointers.</p>\n<p>Mississippi State is scheduled to open the season against Tennessee Tech at 6:30 p.m. Central on Monday, Nov. 2, at Humphrey Coliseum. SEC Network+ will stream the game through the ESPN app.</p>\n<p><em>Source: <a href=\"https://hailstate.com/news/2026/10/12/mens-basketball-hubbard-secures-all-sec-preseason-media-first-team\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mississippi State Athletics</a></em></p>\n<p><em>Correction: An earlier version incorrectly identified Josh Hubbard as a linebacker. He is a men’s basketball guard.</em></p>",
        "tags": [
          1724,
          55,
          1019,
          135
        ]
