        "title": "Mississippi State Sweeps South Carolina in Volleyball",
        "content": "<p>Mississippi State swept South Carolina in four sets Saturday to extend its winning streak at home. The Bulldogs improved to 10-4 overall and 2-0 in the SEC, according to school officials.</p>\n<p><em>Source: <a href=\"https://hailstate.com/news/2026/10/11/volleyball-bulldogs-sweep-the-gamecocks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Original Article</a></em></p>\n",
        "excerpt": "<p>Mississippi State extended its winning streak at home with a four-set victory over South Carolina.</p>\n"
      },
      "patch": {
        "title": "Mississippi State Sweeps South Carolina in Volleyball",
        "excerpt": "Mississippi State swept South Carolina 3-0 on Sunday, Oct. 11, improving to 13-3 overall and 3-2 in SEC play.",
        "content": "<p>Mississippi State swept South Carolina in three sets Sunday, Oct. 11, in Starkville, winning 25-21, 25-14 and 25-19. The Bulldogs improved to 13-3 overall and 3-2 in the Southeastern Conference.</p>\n<p>State rallied from a 12-7 deficit in the opening set and a 6-1 deficit in the third to remain unbeaten at home. The Bulldogs finished with 48 kills and 12 blocks, compared with South Carolina’s 35 kills and six blocks.</p>\n<p>McKenna Yates led Mississippi State with 12 digs. Cayley Hanson recorded 21 assists and Erin Kline added 17. The Bulldogs are scheduled to visit Missouri at 6 p.m. Wednesday, Oct. 14, with coverage on SEC Network.</p>\n<p><em>Source: <a href=\"https://hailstate.com/news/2026/10/11/volleyball-bulldogs-sweep-the-gamecocks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mississippi State Athletics</a></em></p>\n<p><em>Correction: The match was played Sunday, Oct. 11, and ended in three sets. Mississippi State’s post-match records were 13-3 overall and 3-2 in SEC play.</em></p>"
      },
