        "title": "Postseason Baseball Begins as October Arrives",
        "content": "<p>The calendar has turned to October, signaling the start of postseason baseball.</p>\n<p><em>Source: <a href=\"https://hailstate.com/news/2026/10/11/baseball-statetotheshow-update-october-11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Original Article</a></em></p>\n",
        "excerpt": "<p>With October here, the baseball postseason is underway, marking the start of the playoff chase.</p>\n"
      },
      "patch": {
        "title": "Mississippi State Alumni Lowe and Woodruff Featured in October Baseball Update",
        "excerpt": "Mississippi State’s Oct. 11 professional baseball update highlights Nathaniel Lowe’s postseason with Cleveland and Brandon Woodruff’s recovery in Milwaukee.",
        "content": "<p>Mississippi State’s Oct. 11 professional baseball update highlights former Bulldogs Nathaniel Lowe and Brandon Woodruff as their clubs continue through the postseason.</p>\n<p>Lowe joined Cleveland in a late-season trade and helped the Guardians win the American League Central, according to the school’s report. He went 2-for-4 with two singles and a walk against the Chicago White Sox in Game 4 of the American League Division Series on Oct. 8.</p>\n<p>Woodruff’s Milwaukee Brewers won the National League Central. Mississippi State reported that the right-hander was rehabilitating a shoulder injury and hoped to return as a reliever if Milwaukee reached the World Series.</p>\n<p>The update lists 51 former Mississippi State players in professional baseball during 2026. Its player-by-player report covers major-league and minor-league performances.</p>\n<p><em>Source: <a href=\"https://hailstate.com/news/2026/10/11/baseball-statetotheshow-update-october-11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mississippi State Athletics</a></em></p>"
      },
